STEP 1: Indexed job with per-index retries
------------------------------------------
vi indexed-retries.yaml

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: shards
spec:
  completionMode: Indexed
  completions: 6
  parallelism: 3
  backoffLimitPerIndex: 1
  maxFailedIndexes: 2
  ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 600
  template:
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      containers:
      - name: worker
        image: busybox:1.36
        command:
        - sh
        - -c
        - |
          echo "shard $JOB_COMPLETION_INDEX starting"
          if [ "$JOB_COMPLETION_INDEX" = "4" ]; then echo "bad data in shard 4"; exit 1; fi
          sleep 3; echo "shard $JOB_COMPLETION_INDEX done"

k apply -f indexed-retries.yaml
k get pods -l job-name=shards -w
k get job shards -o jsonpath='completed={.status.completedIndexes} failed={.status.failedIndexes}{"\n"}'

Shard 4 fails twice (1 retry) and is marked failed; the others finish.
The Job fails overall (an index failed) but you know EXACTLY which.


STEP 2: podFailurePolicy: stop on a real bug
--------------------------------------------
vi pod-failure-policy.yaml

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: pfp
spec:
  backoffLimit: 6
  podFailurePolicy:
    rules:
    - action: FailJob
      onExitCodes:
        containerName: worker
        operator: In
        values: [42]
  template:
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      containers:
      - name: worker
        image: busybox:1.36
        command: ["sh", "-c", "echo 'config is invalid'; exit 42"]

k apply -f pod-failure-policy.yaml
k get pods -l job-name=pfp       # only ONE pod, no retries
k describe job pfp | tail -4     # PodFailurePolicy reason

Change exit code to 1 and re-run: now it retries up to backoffLimit.


